WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
hosts the Emmy

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Peabody Award-winning show
"Last Week Tonight."

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.637 line:92%
Not a single Oscar, though

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody talks about that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not even nominated.
Snubbed.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:12.612
Airs Sunday nights on HBO and is
available to stream on HBO Max

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
our friend, John Oliver.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, John?
-Yeah, where's my Oscar?

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I was --

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.220 line:92%
I was the voice of Vanity Smurf.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
If that's not Oscar-worthy
what is?

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.025
-You've done a lot of voice work
and not a single --

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-Nothing.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:29.462 size:84% position:42%
I've been Vanity Smurf,
I've been a porcupine,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.764 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I've been a bird.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come on.
That's -- that's range.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's --
Also, talking about range,

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was watching "A Closer Look"
then as you were doing it.

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-For someone who insists,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I don't do impression
at 'SNL,'"

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way you transition
from Kevin McCarthy to Ted Cru

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.281
to Lindsey Graham, it was like
Rich Little at the Bellagio.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:52.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was smooth.
So smooth.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what?
I -- I certainly am gettin

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little
"at the Bellagio" response..

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
...here from my studio crew.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just cutlery?
-You know, I look back,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.130
and I feel like Lorne just
did not recognize my talent.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think...
-Yeah.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:08.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...were he ever
to stumble upon this show...

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...you know?
-If he does --

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.606
Well, we know that won't happen.
But if he is watching,

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:14.174 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it's not about --

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's not sounding like them,
it's embodying.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was Daniel Day Lewis
doing impressions.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
The spirit
of all three men transition --

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't do impressions."
-Yeah.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, it's hard.
'Cause, you know, I come hom

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
from a long day's work,
and I have to say to my wife

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.956 line:92%
"Alexi, I'm Ted right now.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.357 line:92%
I'm gonna need some time.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna need time to --
Seth -- Seth's not here yet.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.563
-When you're reading a -- when
you're reading a story to Ashe

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.165
does he ever say, "And now
as Kevin McCarthy, please?

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Sure.
I just need 15 minutes."

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:44.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
"First, Dad, do Jim Jordan

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
telling me about
Curious George."

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Hey, we're --

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's what every child wants
isn't it?

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do it as Jim Jordan."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want --
I just want this story

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
to contextually have
a very different memory for me

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the future.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've complimented you
time and time again

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
during this difficult year
on your choice to do your show

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the beautiful limbo
that you're in front of now.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
But yet audiences might be
making their way back.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.630 line:92%
How are you feeling about that

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.831 line:92%
-I mean, you know, it was --

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:17.337
it was weird to be without the
for about a show and a half.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.205
-Yep.
-And then, honestly, I've got --

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.908
I have got used to it, if I'm --
if I'm totally honest.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I generally barrel
through them anyway,

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.814
also as someone who did stand-up
for a long time.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am --
I did stand-up in Britain,

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I am used
to delivering jokes to silence

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's almost
how I'm more comfortable.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So it's the sound

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I anticipate,
and when it comes back,

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually, I feel nothing.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:43.062
Well, I think that you and I
are similar in that almost -

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
when a joke goes too well,
we think...

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...collectively the audienc

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
is wrong, and we then
begin to doubt ourselves.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There was --
I will say there are --

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:54.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
Normally, the happiest you wil
see me in a split second

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
is if a joke I've loved
has just bombed.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think --
I feel like I've seen

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:00.346
the same with you where it's -
your face will kind of glow --

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-...as you send the joke

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.584
that you -- that you love
to its inevitable death.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just --
The only thing that is --

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:09.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is going to be really
useful for us is occasionally,

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we occasionally do
something very big,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:14.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
like unveil a 6,000-pound cake
to antagonize

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.862 line:92%
the leader of Turkmenistan

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.498 size:88% position:44%
if you do that without
an audience in the room,

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.599 line:92%
you look like a crazy person

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:20.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That's true.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.404
You guys do have that ability to
go grand every once in a while

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And that necessitates

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:29.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
some kind of sound of joy,
not just a kind of...

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Coughing ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:36.382
-Yeah. Now do you know all you
crew's coughs at this point?

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.518
-Well, see, I'm still not
operating with a crew...

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-...so I -- there is --

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only sound I hear
is my own voice

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:45.959
echoing back at me from th
wall, so I hear nothing.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I think I got the right --

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think 10 people
is about right.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:54.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Honestly, I -- doing the
Edinburgh festival for years

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.570
I performed to a lot less
than 10 a lot of times.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.605 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can honestly --
I can honestly say,

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.842 size:81% position:41%
the first couple years
I was doing Edinburgh,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you walk up
to your stage manager --

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
If it was double figures,
I was like, "It's happening.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:11.784 size:81% position:41%
This is show business.
10 separate people?"

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.954
-My old comedy partner and I
once did a show in Chicago

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:19.726
for nine people, and seven
of them were blood relations

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.195 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:25.999
-I had --
I had 100% walkout in Edinburgh.

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you really?
-Four people --

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.701 line:92%
Four people in the audience.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We got four in tonight?
Okay, great."

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:33.339
After about 10 minutes in,
I'm doing an hour, two leave

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now I've got two people
and it's a couple.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is where
it gets sadistic.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
The guy gets up, says,
"I'm going to the toilet."

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.949 size:84% position:42%
I'm like, "You wouldn't
do this to your wife."

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's looking at him,
going, "Don't.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is --
This is an abandonment issue."

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:50.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
He leaves. She stays
for about 20 more minutes.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:54.460
And I see her hand going dow
to the floor to pick up her bag.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Are you leaving?"
And she said, "Yeah."

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:59.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I will never, ever forget

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:03.536 size:78% position:39%
the sound of the door
closing behind her.

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.104 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, that's --
John, they really didn't

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
like the show because --
-Really didn't.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, for them to be able
to know that you knew...

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I really feel --
I think about what

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
she must have been
going through a lot,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.686
because she must have thought --
she must have calculated,

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
"There's about half an hou
of this show left.

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:24.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is --
What I'm about to do

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
could haunt me
for the rest of my life,

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:28.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's half an hour more
I can't do it."

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:32.398 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you have
a glow about yourself?

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:37.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
Vaccinated, my friend?
-Yes.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got my first --
I got my first shot.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:43.109
So I was very -- Yeah, I'm very,
very happy about it, obviously

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:46.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No -- I -- When I --

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:48.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I got my first shot..
-Yeah.

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:49.782 line:92%
-...the nurse was, I think

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:52.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little surprised
at how happy I was.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.086 size:88% position:44% line:92%
The same happen for you?

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:55.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was absolutely
the case for me.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:58.658 size:88% position:44%
I went in, I was kind of
shaking with excitement.

00:05:58.658 --> 00:05:59.625 line:92%
And she said, "How do you feel?"

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went,
"I'm really, really happy.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so excited about this.
And she said, "Why?"

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it kind of -- it kind of
hit me a little bit odd.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
Think, you know,
"Have you turned on the news

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know why we're all here?
And then she --

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.639 line:92%
I said, "Well, I'm just excite

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause the pandemic
has been really bad."

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said,
"You're not afraid of needles?

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, again --
Again, I don't love them,

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.850 line:92%
but it has been really bad

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:27.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I still see this
as a net positive.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.721 line:92%
Don't ruin the moment for me

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:31.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I -- I remember two thing
when I got my shot.

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:35.895
One, I -- I got a little -
I got a little choked up.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:38.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-And I said to my nurse,

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm never gonna
forget your name."

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:43.069
And the other thing is,
that I do not remember her name.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:48.508 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:50.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember that I forgot it.
-Yeah.

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:53.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, that's -- that's the mos
important thing, isn't it?

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.414 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have a lot more
to ask you about.

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:56.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"It was important to me
in the moment

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.217 line:92%
and I forgot all the lessons."

00:06:58.217 --> 00:06:59.786 line:92%
It feels like, on a macro scale,

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:02.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is what I worry about
with this pandemic,

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
that exactly what you
experienced is going to happen

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:09.929
All the key lessons that wer
put absolutely, blindingly

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:12.532 size:78% position:39%
unblinkingly in front
of people's eyes --

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, let's make a change.
Let's make a change.

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:18.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need to -- we need
to look at environmentally

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
how we're handling things
around the world

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:21.741 size:84% position:42%
to not let a pandemic
like this happen again.

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's over,
and, yeah, "What was that?

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:24.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was something
to do with bats.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:26.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
They like grapes.

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who can stay mad at them?"
[ Laughter ]

